<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112871" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωσφορ-ία</span></b> , ἡ, Astron.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rising and shining</i> of
			the moon or planets <i>when they have drawn away more than</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				15o
			</span></i>
			<i>from the sun,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Serapio
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				8(4).227
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				76
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.Astr.
				1.20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Archit., in
			pl., <i>lights</i> (i.e. windows, etc.) of a building, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHamb.</u>
				15.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
